SUMMARY: Sew So Girls Can Go to School
DESCRIPTION:Join Rotary Toronto Sunrise and help sew menstrual pads for g
 irls in the Dominican Republic and support girl's education in the Domini
 can Republic. Because your period shouldn't put a period in your educatio
 n.\n\nThe group will be working away at 44 Carleton Street Toronto\, in t
 he Party Room on the second floor.\n\nDon't know how to sew or have equip
 ment? No worries\, everything will be provided\; plenty of help needed cu
 tting fabrics. Or you can learn how to sew if you want!\n\nRotarian Janet
  Thorsteinson has been organizing Sew So Girls Can Go to School events fo
 r years\, and will be bringing sewing machines\, supplies and teaching th
 roughout the event.\n\nIf you do have any fabric at home\, old t-shirts\,
  sheets etc. made from cotton or microfibre (really anything that is soft
  and comfortable) it would be much appreciated. And if you have a sewing 
 machine you would like to bring\, please do (recommend bringing a power c
 ord as well if you have one).\n\nQuestions? Reach out to Lori at lori.bra
 zier@gmail.com mailto:lori.brazier@gmail.com and sign up on Eventbrite he
 re https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/sew-so-girls-can-go-to-school-tickets-2003
 923553292?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true .
CATEGORIES:rotary,girl's-education,volunteer,toronto
